# Copy to cluster.env and edit. Sourced by bash (lib.sh) on the admin machine and on every VM.
# This file holds only SITE settings (names, users, network, ids, paths).
# Everything that depends on the size of the VM (memory, cores, heaps) lives in profiles/<VM_PROFILE>.env.
# Hostnames must resolve on every VM and on the admin machine (DNS or /etc/hosts).
#
# Default layout (what the Azure quota allows: 6 vCPUs): 3 VMs with 2 vCPU / 8 GiB each.
#   spark-master : Spark master + NFS server + 1 Kafka broker (Docker container) + Spark drivers   (Standard_D2as_v4)
#   spark-w1     : one Spark worker, 1 executor of 2 cores                                          (Standard_D2s_v4)
#   spark-w2     : one Spark worker, 1 executor of 2 cores                                          (Standard_D2s_v4)
# One broker means replication factor 1: a broker or VM failure takes Kafka down. Fine for a trial, not for production.
#
# Bigger layout (more quota): VM_PROFILE=vm_8gb_4cpu, KAFKA_BROKER_COUNT=3 and SPARK_WORKER_HOSTS=(spark-w1 .. spark-w4).
# Put the settings of that layout in cluster.env; nothing else changes.

# ---- VM size ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Selects infra/cluster/profiles/<VM_PROFILE>.env: memory, cores, Kafka heap, executor sizes.
#   vm_8gb_2cpu   2 vCPU /  8 GiB per VM   (default; Azure Standard_D2as_v4 / Standard_D2s_v4)
#   vm_8gb_4cpu   4 vCPU /  8 GiB per VM   (Azure Standard_F4s_v2; sized for 3 brokers on the master)
#   vm_16gb_4cpu  4 vCPU / 16 GiB per VM   (Azure Standard_D4s_v5)
VM_PROFILE="${VM_PROFILE:-vm_8gb_2cpu}"                    # an environment variable of the same name wins (used by the tests)
# To change a single value without a new profile, set it here, e.g.:
#   SPARK_EXECUTOR_MEMORY=3g
# A value set in this file wins over the profile.

# ---- Topology -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
KAFKA_HOST=spark-master                                    # VM that runs the broker container(s); must not be a worker
SPARK_MASTER_HOST=spark-master
SPARK_WORKER_HOSTS=(spark-w1 spark-w2)
NFS_SERVER_HOST=spark-master                               # may be any Spark VM; the master is the simplest choice
SSH_USER=azureuser                                         # needs key-based ssh and passwordless sudo (Azure default admin user)
NFS_NETWORK=10.0.0.0/24                                    # CIDR of the VMs allowed to mount the share (subnet of spark-vnet)

# ---- Versions (frozen in CLAUDE.md) -------------------------------------------------------
KAFKA_VERSION=3.7.0                                        # Docker image apache/kafka:3.7.0
SPARK_VERSION=3.5.1
SPARK_HADOOP_PROFILE=hadoop3

# ---- Kafka (KRaft in Docker, host networking) -----------------------------------------------
# KAFKA_BROKER_COUNT: 1 (default; replication factor 1, min ISR 1) or 3 (replication factor 3, min ISR 2).
# Broker n listens on clients KAFKA_PORT_BASE + 100*(n-1)  (9092, 9192, 9292)
#                  and controller KAFKA_PORT_BASE + 1 + 100*(n-1)  (9093, 9193, 9293).
KAFKA_BROKER_COUNT="${KAFKA_BROKER_COUNT:-1}"              # an environment variable of the same name wins (used by the tests)
KAFKA_CLUSTER_ID=                                          # run ./gen_cluster_id.sh once; same value for all brokers
KAFKA_PORT_BASE=9092
KAFKA_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/kafka/data                         # host dir; broker n uses <dir>/broker-n
KAFKA_LOG_RETENTION_HOURS=24                               # same as infra/docker-compose.yml

# ---- Shared storage (NFS) -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The repo lives on the share, at the SAME path on every node, because score_job.py puts the repo
# root on the workers' PYTHONPATH and the jobs write checkpoints/ and data/ under the repo root.
SHARED_DIR=/srv/spark-shared
REPO_DIR=/srv/spark-shared/Anomaly-Detection
SPARK_UID=1500                                             # same uid/gid for the 'spark' user on every VM
SPARK_GID=1500

# ---- Python on Spark nodes ----------------------------------------------------------------
PYTHON_BIN=python3.11                                      # contract: Python 3.11 on driver and workers
VENV_DIR=/opt/anomaly-venv                                 # local disk, identical path on every Spark node
INSTALL_ML=yes                                             # torch 2.3.1 CPU (score_job loads the autoencoder on workers)
# OMP_NUM_THREADS / MKL_NUM_THREADS / OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS are fixed to 1 by 30_spark_node.sh: every executor
# core already runs one Python worker, so extra BLAS threads would oversubscribe the cores.
